# Pairs with AtomicOnOwner. A prepare the old copy accepts while a resize
# forwards is not mirrored into the resized copy, so a batch partly prepared
# after the snapshot has a bucket there for one key only, and once the commit
# is decided the resized copy reads it torn.
MODULE: AtomicOnOwnerPrepareNotMirrored
TARGET: AtomicOnOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a prepare during a resize is not mirrored, so the resized copy reads the batch torn
PERTURBS: SagaPrepare

--- FIND
                         IF j = k /\ <<x, y>> \in Landing(c, s, k)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the prepare lands only where it was routed.
                         IF j = k /\ <<x, y>> = <<c, s>>
--- END
